INT. ABANDONED LIGHTHOUSE - LENS ROOM - NIGHT

Wind howls through broken glass. A crushed lantern lies on its side. DETECTIVE NADIA KOROMA, 40s, kneels by a body-shaped tarp. UNIFORM OFFICER TREVOR LANE, 20s, holds a flashlight. HARBORMASTER OSWALD PRIEST, 60s, stands dripping in the doorway.

NADIA
Time of death?

TREVOR
Coroner says midnight.

OSWALD
Midnight? I was here at midnight.

NADIA
You were here?

OSWALD
Checking the light. It was out.

TREVOR
It's always out.

NADIA
Mr. Priest, did you see anyone?

Footsteps on the spiral stair. DR. PHILIPPA ACHTERBERG, 50s, in a rain slicker, climbs into the room, medical bag in hand.

DR. ACHTERBERG
Don't touch the tarp.

NADIA
Doctor.

OSWALD
That's not the coroner.

DR. ACHTERBERG
I'm his sister. I came for the body.

NADIA
Your brother's dead?

Achterberg lowers the bag. Oswald looks at the floor. Trevor looks at Nadia.
